],[30029,41.7,1985,65,89,19],[30030,51.3,1985,69,89,21],[30328,45.9,2013,60,86,21],[30329,41.4,1985,63,86,20],[30330,44.5,1985,66,88,22]],"links":[["Marion County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/oregon/marion-county"],["ARC or PLC in Marion County","/arc-plc/oregon/marion-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 18 grids in Marion County, July to August came in under 90% of normal in 40 of 75 years since 1951, more than any other pair. It is also the driest pair at 1.33 inches normal, and in 2025 it ran 33% of normal. So far in 2026, May to June is at 63% and June to July at 75% on the middle of the grids. Grid 29728 had its driest year in 2013 at 59%.</p>"}
